WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.610
- Afternoon, Donna!

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:03.394
Love what you've done with your fur.

00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:06.453
- [Donna] Oh, you, same as it always is.

00:00:06.453 --> 00:00:07.669
(gasping)

00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:09.289
- Huh?

00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:10.839
(gasping)

00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:11.988
Uh oh.

00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:14.370
(gasping)

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.920
- Oh, wow, look at this!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.130
We're briefcase buddies!

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.540
It's like finding a matching snowflake.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.660
- It's an unremarkable attache,
sold in most major stores.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.600
- And we both bought it.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.920
Plus, to end up sitting next
to each other like this?

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.143
I mean, wow, I'm just gonna say, wow.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.400
Here is your ticket,
and here is your change.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.720
- That's my wallet!

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.630
- Good news, we've got 77 bruckles left.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:44.463
- We?

00:00:44.463 --> 00:00:45.671
There is no "we"!

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:46.740
- [Train Conductor] All aboard!

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.433
- This is so us!

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.863
I could watch you watch paint for days.

00:01:00.302 --> 00:01:03.220
(imitates radio crackle) Best
friend to super best friend,

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.800
what is our plan, over?
(imitates radio crackle)

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.630
- My plan is to find us some ties.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.783
You stay put.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.454
What?

00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:21.058
- (imitates radio crackle)
You didn't say "over", over.

00:01:21.058 --> 00:01:21.891
(imitates radio crackle)

00:01:21.891 --> 00:01:24.960
- That's because I am not
an insane person, over.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.610
There's no way out, Sam.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.960
We have no food.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.800
It's freezing, we won't
even survive the night,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.760
and I'm stuck here with you!

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.810
- There you go, now you're
looking on the bright side!

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.570
This calls for a celebration,

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.210
and I've been saving a bottle of fizzy pop

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.673
for just such an occasion.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.350
That is totally not you.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.517
(yelling)

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.488
See, all you needed was
a little bit of hope.

00:01:55.488 --> 00:01:58.763
Luckily, you had a hope
man in your corner!

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:00.900
- [Narrator] Guy wouldn't admit it,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.150
but he did need some hope.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.783
And a hope man is helpful,
even if he's a dope.

00:02:08.947 --> 00:02:13.870
- Tell me, how does it feel
to be so yipping lucky?

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.340
- You, sir, are about to find out.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.594
Can you feel that?

00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:20.860
How about now?

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.530
- What are you doing?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.513
- It's happening!

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.793
My luck is rubbing off on you!

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.510
- It's me, Guy, with a mustache.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.440
- Nice to meet you, guy with a mustache,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.820
I'm Sam with a jail hat.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.710
What can I do for you, perfect stranger?

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:37.543
- No!

00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:44.510
- (gasps) I knew you'd come back!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.290
I saw you get into that cab,

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.957
but I knew you couldn't
abandon your best friend!

00:02:48.957 --> 00:02:51.540
- What's the plan to bust you out of here?

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.080
- Hmm, feels like a two-man job to me,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.130
if you know what I mean.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.070
- You mean, uh uh?

00:02:59.070 --> 00:02:59.903
- Uh huh.

00:02:59.903 --> 00:03:01.920
- Ah hah hah!
- Ah hah hah hah!

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.514
- Oh, hoho!
- Oh, hoho, ho!

00:03:03.514 --> 00:03:05.597
(laughs)

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:13.120
- Hey, Guy, what a big surprise!

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.510
- So what's the plan?

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.370
- Plan, I don't have a plan.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.070
- But the thing where you
were like (imitates laughing)

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.863
And I was like (imitates laughing)

00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:23.720
- Oh yeah, that was funny!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.949
Good times.

00:03:24.949 --> 00:03:27.116
(panting)

00:03:30.348 --> 00:03:32.681
(straining)

00:03:35.464 --> 00:03:37.070
(laughing)

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.307
- Sam, I just wanna say--

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:43.259
- (sniffs) That was so touching.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.844
(yelling)

00:03:48.844 --> 00:03:51.094
(whooping)

00:03:52.955 --> 00:03:55.020
- Yeah, that's my best friend,

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.540
always ready to lend
a helping hand or two.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.160
- Didn't you guys just meet?

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.840
- And didn't you guys just meet?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.520
Think about it.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.902
- Um...

00:04:05.902 --> 00:04:08.069
(yelling)

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.280
- Everything okay?

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.540
- Uh, no, I mean, yes, I mean,

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.925
everything is a-oh-fine, right Guy?

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:22.910
(imitating Guy) Uh,
yeah, everything's fine.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.240
By the way, Miss Shelley,
have I ever told you

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.722
that you smell like flowers and cupcakes?

00:04:27.722 --> 00:04:32.722
- So, you really think I smell
like flowers and cupcakes?

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:33.723
- Huh?

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.113
- I never told anybody this before,

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:45.123
when I was very little my
mom left me at an orphanage.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.230
It's always just been me.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.053
I mean, at least until I met you.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.000
I've been trying to find
her all these years,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.263
so I can ask why, you know?

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.383
Why she gave me up.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.960
I'm sure it's a good reason,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.402
I just really wanna know.

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:10.735
(sad music)

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.345
- Keep trying, Sam.

00:05:20.345 --> 00:05:23.012
(hopeful music)

00:05:28.864 --> 00:05:33.864
- I will.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.056
- Guy!

00:05:41.056 --> 00:05:42.370
(growling)

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.820
- Sam, no, as your best friend
I'm telling you to flee!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.600
Save Jenkins!

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.100
- Hold up, did you just
say we're best friends?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.133
- Yes, now go!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.123
- For Jenkins!

00:05:56.284 --> 00:05:59.187
Whoah, there's my boo!

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.383
(growls)

00:06:01.383 --> 00:06:03.380
What did I miss?

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.890
- Stop talking.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.120
- But Guy--
- No!

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.840
Everything you've ever told me is a lie!

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.183
You're a wanted criminal!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.990
- It's nice to be wanted?

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.488
Okay, I know you're not happy about

00:06:18.488 --> 00:06:20.610
the little setback in our relationship,

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.800
- We have no relationship.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.400
I've tried you as a
friend, and you don't fit.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.586
You don't fit anybody,

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:30.643
not even your own mother.

00:06:30.643 --> 00:06:32.976
(sad music)

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:35.633
- I'm sorry.

00:06:35.633 --> 00:06:37.933
- No, no, no, you're right.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.273
- [Guy] No!

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.920
The truth is, you're the
best friend I've ever had.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.060
- I'm the only friend you've ever had.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.303
- Yes, but that still makes you the best.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.180
- You know, the only thing
that's ever hurt as much

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.230
as missing my mom,

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.560
was what you said about her leaving me.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.100
- I know, but is there any way

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.283
you could at least try to forgive me?

00:07:11.351 --> 00:07:12.601
- I don't know.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.450
- [Narrator] It's not easy to warm up

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.163
a friendship gone cold.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.210
It takes something big, something huge,

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.050
something bold.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:26.050
(Mischievous music)

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.080
- Guy, what are you doing?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.443
- This is how much I wanna be your friend.

00:07:34.666 --> 00:07:36.833
(chewing)

00:07:43.198 --> 00:07:44.031
Mmm!

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:50.150
Say, I like green eggs and ham!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.052
I do!

00:07:51.052 --> 00:07:53.802
(cheerful music)

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.360
- Okay, boys, what can I getcha?

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.360
- Hmm, tough call, let me
see, lots of choices here.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.933
- Two orders of green
eggs and ham, please.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.623
I like them.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.703
A conclusion I would have
eventually come to on my own.

00:08:20.091 --> 00:08:20.924
- Mm hmm.

00:08:22.014 --> 00:08:25.540
- (sighs) thank you for
getting me to try them, okay?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.817
Thank you, Sam, I am.

00:08:27.817 --> 00:08:31.310
[Narrator] This was the
story of Sam, and of Guy.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.983
A story about giving new things a try.

